Case Study Opportunities, GPTBot News + More 
 ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌ ‌


Hey there! 

Maddie here from Originality.AI! 

We have three things we wanted to discuss in this email. 

* We invite you to share your use case with our community! 

* We look at GPTBot and how top websites are responding to it. 

* Our commentary on GPTBot..

**Featured Case Study **

We love chatting with our customers and have been gaining some really
great insights on how you are leveraging our tools within your
processes. 

We've showcased one of our clients, BrandBuilders.io,
<https://jonhaver.lt.acemlnb.com/Prod/link-tracker?redirectUrl=aHR0cHMlM0ElMkYlMkZwbGF0Zm9ybS5vcGVuYWkuY29tJTJGZG9jcyUyRmdwdGJvdA%3D%3D&a=%7C%7C798597961%7C%7C&account=jonhaver.activehosted.com&email=PJj8vz75nOIubmRpE3pMpUIyuJo46gIwyB3tLG%2Fh95Sjf9leVKI6YOiNaZo%3D%3AYPERlgjHNBhC8ZKZdCPnPtR%2F1AV5oNb%2F&s=c2aa77b6f0a29bb9a1c1a13f88329783&i=1952A2116A61A30075%3E%2015%20days%20ago%20and%20we%0Aconducted%20a%20study%20to%20see%20how%20websites%20are%20responding.%C2%A0%0A%0A%2A%2ASummary%20of%20Key%20Findings%3A%C2%A0%2A%2A%0A%0A%2A%209.2%25%20of%20the%20Top%201000%20Websites%20Have%20Blocked%20GPTBot%20in%20its%20First%2014%20Days%0A%0A%2A%2069%20of%20the%20759%20sites%20that%20we%20were%20able%20to%20check%20are%20blocking%20GPTBot%0A%0A%2A%20The%20First%20&sig=83pnc5nhEkiLrVpCS7wb64AgddzNHEPCEH7XFz8HUN6W&iat=1692911427"Top 100" Website to Block GPTBot was Reuters.com

* Top 6 Websites That Blocked GPTBot Within The First 2 Weeks:
Amazon.com, Quora.com, NYTimes.com, Shutterstock.com, Wikihow.com,
CNN.com

* The Most Popular Websites Are More Likely to Block GPTBot

* 15% of the top 100 Websites Checked Are Blocking GPTBot compared to
9.2% of the Top 1000 websites.

* The % of Websites Blocking GPTBot is Increasing at ~5% Per Week

Read the full study here:
https://jonhaver.lt.acemlnb.com/Prod/link-tracker?redirectUrl=aHR0cHMlM0ElMkYlMkZvcmlnaW5hbGl0eS5haSUyRmJsb2clMkZzdHVkeS13ZWJzaXRlcy1ibG9ja2luZy1ncHRib3Q%3D&a=%7C%7C798597961%7C%7C&account=jonhaver.activehosted.com&email=PJj8vz75nOIubmRpE3pMpUIyuJo46gIwyB3tLG%2Fh95Sjf9leVKI6YOiNaZo%3D%3AYPERlgjHNBhC8ZKZdCPnPtR%2F1AV5oNb%2F&s=c2aa77b6f0a29bb9a1c1a13f88329783&i=1952A2116A61A30076%3E%0A%0A%2A%2A%2A%2AOur%20Comments%20on%20GPTBot%3A%2A%2A%2A%2A%0A%0AWe%20wonder%20if%20there%20is%20a%20potential%20downside%20of%20blocking%20GPTBot.%0A%0AAs%20ChatGPT%20gets%20smarter%2Fcozier%20with%20the%20internet%2C%20it%20could%20start%20to%0Aresemble%20a%20search%20engine%20by%20guiding%20users%20to%20direct%20links%20references%0Afrom%20the%20web.%20We%20wonder%20if%20blocking%20GPTBot%20could%20essentially%20be%20like%0Asaying%20&sig=2jQ9HFjUEjvjhVv7xEaPYwoMYD6SbLB9RdK7Cu3VU57c&iat=1692911427'no thanks' to potential visitors. 

Essentially, just as blocking Google could vanish you from a top search
engine, blocking GPTBot could mean waving goodbye to a whole stream of
web traffic, depending on where OpenAI goes with this.

This is all just theory until OpenAI shares more about the purpose of
GPTBot, but we wanted to play devil's advocate as blocking GPTBot does
appear to be a trend that big websites are jumping on quickly. 

Maybe some more thought is required... 

Thanks for reading! 

  

Sent to: patriogabrielpatdu@gmail.com

